BLD-shape_guards_by_phase.content:
Links: prep across the tree it walks (prep §6.2 item 3); geotag and merge at the workspace root at startup (geotag §13;
merge precondition 0a), and through the handoff (geotag §7.2; merge precondition 3). Missing managed folders: prep §6.2
item 7, geotag §13, merge precondition 0c.

DEF-config_areas.content:
The configuration sets, at least: the snapshot policy; which camera groups are phones and which have fixed clocks; the
filename timestamp format; where the tracks are and the thresholds for matching photos to them; the camera-time policy;
the library and how merge places files in it; the managed folders' names; the names of the development subfolders;
and which extensions are which class of media. Each area's detail is in the items of its own section.

DEF-managed_folders.content:
The **managed folders** are the workspace's media folders, each with a fixed role: the **inbox**, where a dump arrives;
the strays folder; **missing metadata**, for media with no capture time; **redundant JPEGs**; **videos by date**;
**photos by date**; and **photos by destination**, the staging the user sorts photos into and merge empties into the
library.

RAT-folder_names_are_places.content:
Each managed folder's name becomes a folder at the workspace's top level. A name holding a separator would put it inside
another; a hidden one would be passed over as a hidden entry; two roles under one name would pour two folders into one;
and the control records' or the quarantine's name would mix media with the records about them.

RAT-snapshot_just_before.content:
A snapshot restores the state just before a plan's changes. Taken before the plan is validated, it may precede a plan
that is then refused; taken outside the lock, another run may change the workspace between it and the first change;
taken after a change, it no longer restores the state before it.

RUL-withdrawal_undoes.content:
Withdrawing a decision SHALL undo its effect, not merely stop asserting it: a manual position withdrawn gives the file
the position it would have had without it — from the tracks, or none; a position derived by the tool is derived again;
a time and a name are recomputed where the file stands, never moving it out of its destination.
